"""1N4148W - fast switching diode, 100 V, 150 mA, SOD-123.

Datasheet: Zhuhai Hongjiacheng Technology (R+O) 1N4148W Rev 2.0, LCSC C7420318
("DIO-DS").

Maximum ratings (DIO-DS p.1, Ta = 25 C): VRRM 100 V, VRMS 75 V, IF(AV) 150 mA,
IFRM 300 mA, IFSM 2.0 A at tp = 1 us and 0.5 A at tp = 1 s, Pd 400 mW,
Tj -55 to +150 C, RthJA 315 C/W.
Characteristics (DIO-DS p.2): VF max 0.715 V at 1 mA, 0.855 V at 10 mA, 1.0 V
at 50 mA, 1.25 V at 150 mA; IR max 25 nA at 20 V, 1.0 uA at 75 V; CT 4.0 pF max
at 0 V; trr 4.0 ns max (IF = IR = 10 mA, Irr = 0.1 IR, RL = 100 ohm).
Polarity (p.1): the cathode line marks the cathode end.

Pins: pad 1 anode (A), pad 2 cathode (K). The footprint (LCSC/EasyEDA
SOD-123_L2.7-W1.6-LS3.7-FD, Altium MicrasLib) marks the cathode at pad 2 with
its silkscreen arrow and bar, and its STEP model has the cathode band at pad 2.
Pads 0.88 x 0.96 mm at x = +/-1.61 mm (2.34 mm gap). DIO-DS p.3 "Suggested Pad
Layout" asks for 0.91 mm min pad length (J), 2.36 mm max gap (K) and 1.22 mm
min pad width (M): the gap fits, the pads are 0.03 mm shorter and 0.26 mm
narrower than suggested.

This is the stdlib Rectifier generic's part, packaged because the generic
cannot carry an MPN and numbers the KiCad SOD-123 footprint cathode-first
(pad 1 = K), the reverse of this footprint.
"""

A = io(Net)
K = io(Net)

Component(
    name="D",
    prefix="D",
    symbol=Symbol(library="1N4148W.kicad_sym"),
    footprint=File("SOD-123_L2.7-W1.6-LS3.7-FD.kicad_mod"),
    part=Part(mpn="1N4148W", manufacturer="Hongjiacheng"),
    pins={
        "A": A,
        "K": K,
    },
)
